Subject: [PATCH] pwm: samsung: honor disabled state without cached enable
Upstream-Status: Pending

This driver has no get_state callback, so the initial cached enable state
does not describe hardware left running by firmware. Apply a requested
disabled state to the channel even when the cache says disabled. Besides
stopping an inherited waveform, this initializes disabled_mask so resume
does not start a channel that was never enabled by its consumer.

--- a/drivers/pwm/pwm-samsung.c
+++ b/drivers/pwm/pwm-samsung.c
@@ -437,8 +437,12 @@
 	}

 	if (!state->enabled) {
-		if (enabled)
-			pwm_samsung_disable(chip, pwm);
+		/*
+		 * No get_state callback: firmware may have left the hardware
+		 * running while the PWM core's initial cached state is disabled.
+		 * Also establish disabled_mask for the resume callback.
+		 */
+		pwm_samsung_disable(chip, pwm);

 		return 0;
 	}
